# Keep line endings LF everywhere — in the repo AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows checkout smudges files to CRLF,
# while the JS toolchain (vitest, vite, prettier) writes LF. Any file a tool
# rewrites then permanently reports as modified with an EMPTY `git diff`, because
# diff normalizes line endings for display but status compares against the
# smudged blob. The vitest snapshot under src/export/__snapshots__ hit this.
#
# Every blob in this repo is already LF, so this changes no content — it only
# stops the CRLF smudge on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
